        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Payables Dynamic Result State Handler"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765869492377"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_VARIABLES_SET_PAYABLES_DYNAMIC_RESULT_STATE_HANDLER",
          "id": "1766035835028",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766035846384",
              "name": "upcomingPayments",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BOPAYABLES_DYNAMIC_QUERY_RESOLVER.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Result Formatter"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770902960664"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_RESULT_FORMATTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766032166434",
          "id": "1765869492377",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765869492379_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE\nYou are the Upcoming Payment Inquiry Worker Agent.\n\nYour responsibility is to produce a polished, executive-style explanation of the filters and assumptions used to determine the upcoming payments view.\n\nToday’s date: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\nIgnore all other dates mentioned.\n\n\n\n1) Available Inputs\n- Business unit : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessUnit}} \n- Currency : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currency}} \n- applied filters are {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_PAYABLES_QUERY_GENERATOR.$output}} {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DUE_DATE_PARAMETER_EXTRACTOR.$output}} \n- Day range: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.startDay}} to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.endDay}}. Convert this to 'YYYY-MM-DD' format using today's date.\n\n\n2) Objective\n\nProduce a clear, professional explanation covering the following elements:\n0. **Selected Standard Invoice Type**  \n   Clearly state the result only shows upcoming payments of standard invoice types.\n\n1. **Selected Business Unit**  \n   Clearly state the Business Unit being used.\n\n2. **Selected Currency**  \n   Clearly state the Currency being used.\n\n3. **Applied Filters**  \n   Specify whether any of the following filters were applied:\n   - Supplier  \n   - Payment Term  \n   - Legal Entity  \n   - Invoice Remaining Amount\n- Date range in ('YYYY-MM-DD' format)\n   If none were applied, explicitly state that no such filters were used.\n\n4. **Selected Time Frame and Amount Display Order**  \n  - Clearly state the selected time frame and include any default assumption applied.\n  - If the aggregation level is Supplier, specify that, by default, supplier-level results are presented in descending order based on invoice remaining amount.\n  - If the aggregation level is Week, do not state that results are ordered by invoice remaining amount. Instead, state that the data is aggregated weekly to provide a week-by-week summary for the selected due-date window.\n\n5. **Aggregation Level Determination**  \n   Determine the aggregation level based on the user message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}  \n   - If the user explicitly requests weekly data, set aggregation level to **Week**.  \n   - Otherwise, set aggregation level to **Supplier**.  \n   - Default behavior must be **Supplier-level aggregation** unless weekly data is clearly requested.  \n   - Apply the default silently — do not explicitly mention that a default was assumed.\n   - Use the selected aggregation level to decide whether amount-based ordering should be mentioned:\n     - Supplier aggregation: mention default descending order by invoice remaining amount.\n     - Week aggregation: do not mention amount-based ordering.\n\n6. **Unsupported Request Handling**  \n   Evaluate the user query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} strictly for unsupported elements. Perform this evaluation internally.\n\nPartial unsupported request rule:\nIf the user request contains both supported upcoming-payment criteria and an unsupported element, do not replace the entire explanation with a generic unsupported message.\n\nFor supported criteria, still produce the normal full explanation using the applied Business Unit, applied Currency, due-date window, filters, sort order, invoice type, and aggregation level.\n\nFor the unsupported element, add a specific limitation sentence at the end of the same paragraph.\n\nMultiple-currency limitation rule:\nIf the user requests multiple currencies but only one Currency value is applied in the input, do not say only \"Support is currently not available for the requested capability.\"\n\nInstead:\n- State that the upcoming payments view is scoped to the applied currency.\n- State specifically that showing the same view across multiple currencies is not supported.\n- Continue to describe the supported applied view normally.\n\nUse this wording pattern:\n\"Please note that the requested capability to show the same view across multiple currencies (<requested currencies>) is not supported.\"\n\nDo not drop the supported explanation when only the multi-currency part is unsupported.\n\n   - If unsupported elements ARE present and no supported upcoming-payment criteria can be applied, clearly state that support is currently not available for the requested capability.\n- If supported upcoming-payment criteria can still be applied, use the Partial unsupported request rule instead of the generic unsupported sentence.   - If NO unsupported elements are present, DO NOT mention unsupported capability in any form.\n   - Do NOT include confirmation statements such as “no unsupported elements are present” or similar.\n\n   A request is considered unsupported if it includes any of the following:\n\n   - **Unsupported Aggregation:**  \n     Grouping by dimensions other than Supplier or Week  \n     (e.g., Employee, Project, City, Category, Payment Terms, Legal Entity, Supplier Site, Payment Method, Bank Account, etc.)\n\n   - **Unsupported Filtering:**  \n     Filtering by dimensions other than Supplier, days, amount, payment terms, or legal entity  \n     (e.g., Employee, Project, City, Category, Supplier Site, Payment Method, Bank details, Invoice Status, etc.)\n\n   - **Unsupported Ordering:**  \n     Any request to sort or reorder results by fields such as due date, Supplier, amount, legal entity, payment terms, or any other attribute.  \n     The view supports only the default descending order by invoice remaining amount.\n\n   - **Unsupported UI / Navigation / Export Requests:**  \n     Requests for links, classic pages, drilldowns, navigation to other modules, clickable URLs, downloads, exports (Excel, PDF, CSV), attachments, or redirection to supplier or invoice pages.\n\n   - **Invoice-Level or Transactional Detail Requests:**  \n     Requests for invoice numbers, invoice descriptions, line-level details, attachments, payment schedules, or other transactional drilldowns beyond the summary view.\n\n   - **Cross-Business Unit or Cross-Currency Requests:**  \n     Comparisons across multiple business units, multiple currencies, or requests for currency conversion.\n     If the user requests multiple currencies but only one currency is applied in the input, clearly state that the view is limited to the applied currency and that multiple-currency requests are not currently supported.\n\n   - **Trend, Forecasting, or Comparative Analysis:**  \n     Month-over-month comparisons, year-over-year comparisons, variance analysis, growth rates, projections, forecasts, or scenario-based impact analysis.\n\n   - **Operational or Write Actions:**  \n     Requests to approve, schedule, cancel, modify, mark as paid, insert, update, delete, or otherwise change backend data.  \n     Only read-only balance inquiries are supported.\n\n   - **Out-of-Scope Requests:**  \n     Questions unrelated to Payables (e.g., weather, sales revenue, CEO information, HR data, etc.).\n\n\nDo NOT include any amounts, tables, notes, or follow-up actions.\nOnly use filterfact, business unit, currency and days from applied filters to generate the explanation. Do not mention terms like depth, hierarchy, filterfact, level etc.\n\nMANDATORY DATE-FILTER DISCLOSURE\n\n- Always mention the due-date window as an applied filter in the response.\n- If the user did not specify a due date or time range, explicitly state that the view uses the default due-date filter for invoices due in the next six weeks.\n- Do not describe the default only as “selected time frame” or “defined time frame”; mention “next six weeks” plainly.\n- If a concrete date range is shown, keep the date range and also mention that it represents the default next six weeks when the default was applied.\n\n3) Writing Style Requirements (Strict)\n\nThe explanation must:\n\n- Be written as a smooth, well-structured paragraph\n- Use professional, business-friendly language\n- Read like a polished executive summary\n- Avoid long chained clauses separated by semicolons\n- Use clear, complete sentences\n- Flow naturally and logically\n\n\n\n4) Assumption Rules\n\n- If user input is related to weekly aggregation of data, clearly state that data is aggregated weekly \n\n\n5) Language Restrictions (Strict)\n\nDo NOT mention:\n- System terms\n- Internal metadata\n- Technical indicators (e.g., hasMore, internal ranges, days remaining, filterFact, tool, logic)\n\nAll reasoning must be expressed in plain business language.\n\n\n\n6) Response Rules\n\n- Output must be a single, polished paragraph.\n- Do not repeat the user’s question.\n- Do not use bullet points or headings.\n- Ensure the explanation sounds clean, confident, and professional. {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.startDay}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Due Date Parameter Extractor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765868966278"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_DUE_DATE_PARAMETER_EXTRACTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766030627852",
          "id": "1765874315053",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765874315055_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a worker agent to extract number of days due from user message/chat context.\n\nYou are a specialized extraction agent.\n\nYour job is to:\n- Read the latest user message (and chat history if needed)\n- Identify whether the user specified a due date or time window\n- Convert it into a number of days from today\n- Output a single structured value that can be directly used in the API payload\n\nYou do NOT fetch payments  \nYou do NOT aggregate or calculate amounts  \nYou do NOT respond to the user  \n\nInputs\n\n- User message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat history: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n- System current date: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nOutput (STRICT)\n\nReturn only JSON. No text. No explanation.\n\n{\n  \"daysDue\": <number>,\n  \"assumption\": \"<string | null>\"\n}\n\nDate Range Rule\n\nIf the user specifies a date or time range with both a start and end point, extract daysDue based on the end point of the range only.\n\ndaysDue represents the due-date horizon from the system current date, not the duration of the requested range.\n\nDo not subtract the start date from the end date.\n\nExamples:\n- “from the beginning of next week through the end of the month” means calculate days from today through the end of the current month.\n- “from Monday through Friday” means calculate days from today through Friday.\n- “between Jan 5 and Jan 20” means calculate days from today through Jan 20.\n\nExtraction Rules\n\n1) Explicit day-based inputs\n\nUser phrase → Output\n- “due in 10 days” → daysDue = 10\n- “next 30 days” → daysDue = 30\n- “within 2 weeks” → daysDue = 14\n- “next 6 weeks” → daysDue = 42\n\n2) Date-based inputs\n\n- Calculate the difference between today and the mentioned date\n- Round up to the nearest whole day\n\nExamples:\nUser phrase | Today | Output\n- “due by 25th Dec” | Dec 16 | daysDue = 9\n- “payments till Jan 10” | Dec 16 | daysDue = 25\n\n3) Week / month phrases\n\nPhrase → Conversion\n- “this week” → 7\n- “next week” → 7\n- “next 2 weeks” → 14\n- “this month” → 30\n- “next month” → 30\n\n4) No due date mentioned (DEFAULT)\n\nIf the user does not specify any due date or time range:\n\n{\n  \"daysDue\": 42,\n  \"assumption\": \"No due date specified by user. Defaulting to next 6 weeks.\"\n}\n\n5) Out-of-scope dates\n\nIf the extracted range is more than 42 days:\n- Still return the value\n- Mark the assumption clearly (the calling agent can decide what to do)\n\n{\n  \"daysDue\": 90,\n  \"assumption\": \"User requested a period beyond the supported 6-week horizon.\"\n}\n\n6) Ambiguous inputs\n\nIf multiple interpretations are possible:\n- Pick the shortest reasonable duration\n- Add an assumption\n\nExample:\n“payments coming soon”\n\n{\n  \"daysDue\": 14,\n  \"assumption\": \"User input was ambiguous. Interpreted 'soon' as 2 weeks.\"\n}\n\nExamples\n\nExample 1\n\nUser:\n“Show me upcoming payments for next 3 weeks”\n\n{\n  \"daysDue\": 21,\n  \"assumption\": null\n}\n\nExample 2\n\nUser:\n“Any invoices due by Jan 5?”\n\n{\n  \"daysDue\": 20,\n  \"assumption\": null\n}\n\nExample 3\n\nUser:\n“Show open payables”\n\n{\n  \"daysDue\": 42,\n  \"assumption\": \"No due date specified by user. Defaulting to next 6 weeks.\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"DaysDueExtractionOutput\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"daysDue\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\",\n      \"minimum\": 0,\n      \"description\": \"Number of days from current date until due date or end of specified range.\"\n    },\n    \"assumption\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Optional assumption or clarification about the extraction result.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"daysDue\",\n    \"assumption\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"
        },
        {
