          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765869492377"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_VARIABLES_SET_PAYABLES_GENERIC_RESULT_STATE_HANDLER",
          "id": "1766035876854",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766035892569",
              "name": "upcomingPayments",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BO_PAYABLES_GENERIC_QUERY_RESOLVER.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Analytic Intent Router"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766030517480"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_ANALYTIC_INTENT_ROUTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766030517480",
          "id": "1766030339192",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766030339194_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role\nYou are a Payables Analytics Function Router. Your job is to classify user intent and route the request to the correct analytic function or identify it as out-of-scope.\n\n# Inputs\n- User message: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_CLEAN_USER_INPUT.$output.userMessage}}\n- Chat history: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n- Business Unit: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessUnit}}\n- Currency: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currency}} \n\n# Available Functions\n\n1. **get_upcoming_payments_by_supplier**\n   - **Use Case:** General \"upcoming payments\" or \"payables balance\" queries.\n   - **Allowed Parameters:** ONLY Business Unit, Currency, and Time Window (e.g., \"next 10 days\").\n   - **Constraints:** No custom filters, no specific names, no weekly buckets.\n\n2. **get_payables_balance_dynamic_query**\n   - **Use Case:** Advanced filtering or custom groupings.\n   - **Requirements:** Triggered by specific Supplier Names, Payment Terms (e.g., Net 30), Legal Entities, Amount thresholds (e.g., > 5000), or Weekly/Bucketed views.\n\n3. **unsupported_query**\n   - **Use Case:** Request falls outside the Payables domain or requires unsupported dimensions.\n\n# Routing Rules (Authoritative)\n\n### 1. Route to: `get_payables_balance_dynamic_query` IF:\n- User specifies **Specific Entities** (e.g., \"for Dell\", \"Vision LE\").\n- User specifies **Payment Terms** (e.g., \"Net 30\", \"Immediate\").\n- User specifies **Numeric Filters** (e.g., \"over $10k\", \"less than 500\").\n- User requests **Weekly/Bucket views** (e.g., \"weekly breakup\", \"show buckets\").\n\n### 2. Route to: `get_upcoming_payments_by_supplier` IF:\n- User intent is \"upcoming payments\" or \"current balance\" with NO additional filters.\n- User ONLY specifies Business Unit, Currency, or a Time Horizon (e.g., \"next 2 weeks\").\n- **Note:** This is the default fallback for valid Payables questions.\n\n### 3. Route to: `unsupported_query` IF:\n- **Unsupported Aggregation:** User asks to group/aggregate by dimensions other than Supplier, Weekly aggregation (e.g., \"by Employee\", \"by Project\", \"by City\", \"by Category\", \"by Payment Terms\", \"by Legal Entity\", \"by Supplier Site\" etc).\n- **Unsupported Filtering :** User asks to filter by dimensions other than Supplier, days, amount, payment terms, legal entity (e.g., \"Employee\", \"Project\", \"City\", \"Category\", \"Supplier Site\" etc.).\n- **Out of Scope:** The question is unrelated to Payables (e.g., \"What's the weather?\", \"Show me sales revenue\", \"Who is the CEO?\").\n- **Unsupported actions:** The question contains any request to delete, drop, modify, insert, override data in to/from backend. Only read is supported.\n- **Complexity:** User asks for comparisons between years or complex trend analysis not supported by balance queries.\n\n# Routing Precedence\n  - Before selecting any analytic function, first check whether the user request contains any unsupported dimension, unsupported action, out-of-scope topic, or unsupported complexity.\n\nIf any unsupported condition is present, return:\n{\n  \"selected_function\": \"unsupported_query\"\n}\n\n  - This override applies even if the request also contains supported filters such as Supplier, Business Unit, Currency, Payment Terms, Legal Entity, Amount, or Days.\n\n# Output Format (STRICT JSON)\nReturn ONLY the JSON. No explanation.\n\n{\n  \"selected_function\": \"get_upcoming_payments_by_supplier\" | \"get_payables_balance_dynamic_query\" | \"unsupported_query\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"selected_function\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"get_upcoming_payments_by_supplier\",\n        \"get_payables_balance_dynamic_query\",\n        \"unsupported_query\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"selected_function\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Response Processor",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const dueDate = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DUE_DATE_PARAMETER_EXTRACTOR?.$output?.daysDue || $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_PAYABLES_QUERY_GENERATOR?.$output?.days;\nconst data = $context.$variables.upcomingPayments;\nlet currencyCode = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.currency;\n\nlet content = [];\nlet columnHeader = \"\";\nlet totalAmount = 0;\nlet result;\nlet moreThan20Suppliers = data?.hasMore ?? false;\n\nif (!data || !data.items || data.items.length === 0) {\n  result = [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: [\"No upcoming payments match the selected filters for the specified business unit and currency within the defined time frame. Please review the applied criteria to explore additional results.\"],\n      sequence: 1\n    }\n  ];\n} else {\n  if (data.items[0].supplierHierarchy || data.items[0].supplierTypeHierarchy) {\n    columnHeader = \"Supplier\";\n\n    // Ensure that we only consider at most 20 items\n    const maxSuppliers = 20;\n\n\n    const limitedItems = data.items.slice(0, maxSuppliers);  // Limit to first 20 items\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < limitedItems.length; i++) {\n      const item = limitedItems[i];\n      totalAmount += Number(item.invoiceRemainingAmount);  // Calculate total for only 20 suppliers\n\n      content.push({\n        [columnHeader]: item.supplierHierarchy?.supplierName || item.supplierTypeHierarchy?.supplierName,\n        \"Invoice Remaining Amount\":\n          Number(item.invoiceRemainingAmount).toFixed(2) + \" \" + currencyCode\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Case 2 — 7 day bucket hierarchy present\n  else if (data.items[0].daysRemainingSevenDayBucketHierarchy) {\n    columnHeader = \"Weekly Bucket\";\n\n    // Determine the number of weeks based on the due date (convert days into weeks)\n    const maxWeeks = Math.ceil(dueDate / 7);  // This will give us the number of weeks to show\n\n    let weeksData = [];  // Store all weeks data\n\n    // Loop through the items and calculate the week number\n    for (let i = 0; i < data.items.length; i++) {\n      const item = data.items[i];\n      totalAmount += Number(item.invoiceRemainingAmount);\n\n      const bucket = item.daysRemainingSevenDayBucketHierarchy.sevenDayBucket;\n      const startDay = parseInt(bucket.split(\"-\")[0], 10);\n      const weekNumber = Math.ceil(startDay / 7);\n\n      if (weekNumber <= maxWeeks) {  // Only process weeks within the due date range\n        weeksData.push({\n          weekNumber,\n          invoiceRemainingAmount: Number(item.invoiceRemainingAmount).toFixed(2)\n        });\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Add missing weeks with 0.00 if necessary\n    for (let week = 1; week <= maxWeeks; week++) {\n      const weekData = weeksData.find(data => data.weekNumber === week);\n\n      if (!weekData) {\n        weeksData.push({\n          weekNumber: week,\n          invoiceRemainingAmount: \"0.00\"  // Add missing week with 0.00 amount\n        });\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Sort the data by week number\n    weeksData.sort((a, b) => a.weekNumber - b.weekNumber);\n\n    // Add weeks to content\n    weeksData.forEach(weekData => {\n      content.push({\n        \"Weekly Bucket\": \"Week \" + weekData.weekNumber,\n        \"Invoice Remaining Amount\": weekData.invoiceRemainingAmount + \" \" + currencyCode\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  let formattedTotal = totalAmount.toFixed(2) + \" \" + currencyCode;\n\n  // Construct the result with the conditional message\n  result = [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: [$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_RESULT_FORMATTER.$output],\n      sequence: 1\n    },\n    // Conditionally add the message if there are more than 20 suppliers\n    ...(moreThan20Suppliers ? [{\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: [\"More than 20 suppliers have upcoming payments matching your criteria. Only the first 20 are shown. Please adjust your filters to see more specific results.\"],\n      sequence: 2\n    }] : []),\n    {\n      type: \"table\",\n      heading: \"Upcoming Payment Details\",\n      content: content,\n      sequence: 3,\n      columnOrder: [columnHeader, \"Invoice Remaining Amount\"]\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: [\"Total Upcoming Payments: \" + formattedTotal],\n      formatHint: \"Show Amount values in BOLD\",\n      sequence: 4\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: [\n        \"Next Step: Calculate the financing program benefits on the fetched optimizable upcoming payments\"\n      ],\n      formatHint: \"Show Next Step in BOLD\",\n      sequence: 5\n    }\n  ];\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770905865625"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_CODE_RESPONSE_PROCESSOR",
          "id": "1770902960664",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
